/*
  PDFRender - RISC OS render backend.

  All SWI interfaces below are per the PRMs (RO3 PRM 'Draw',
  'Sprites', 'Font manager', 'ColourTrans' chapters; RO3.5/3.6
  Vol 5a for new-format sprites and the JPEG SWIs):

    Draw_Fill    &40702  R0 path, R1 style, R2 matrix, R3 flatness
    Draw_Stroke  &40704  ... R4 thickness, R5 cap/join, R6 dashes
      - path coords are 1/256 OS unit (our device fix >> 8)
      - element types: 2 move, 8 line, 6 bezier, 5 close, 0 end
      - fill style bits 0-1: 0 nonzero, 2 even-odd (+ &30 plot bits)
    OS_SpriteOp  &2E     +256 name / +512 sprite pointer forms
      15 create, 52 put scaled, 60 switch output, 62 save area size
    Font_FindFont &40081, Font_LoseFont &40082
    Font_Paint   &40086  bit6 matrix (16.16, translation millipoint),
                         bit7 R7 length, bit8 R0 handle
    Font_ScanString &400A1 (millipoints throughout)
    ColourTrans_SetGCOL &40743, ColourTrans_SetFontColours &4074F
    JPEG_Info    &49980, JPEG_PlotScaled &49982

  Millipoint rule: 1 OS unit = 400 millipoints; the sprite is built
  as 180 dpi so 1 pixel = 1 OS unit and Draw/Font output is 1:1.

  Copyright (c) RISC OS Technologies 2026.
